#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:102
msgid "Basic usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:104
msgid ""
"Before you can do anything else, you need to define a schema. For the "
"purposes of this guide, we'll use a simple object schema."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:106
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"import * as z from \"zod\";\n"
"\n"
"const Player = z.object({\n"
"  username: z.string(),\n"
"  xp: z.number(),\n"
"});\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:115
msgid "Parsing data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:117
msgid ""
"Given any Zod schema, use `.parse` to validate an input. If it's valid, "
"Zod returns a strongly-typed _deep clone_ of the input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:119
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Player.parse({ username: \"billie\", xp: 100 });\n"
"// => returns { username: \"billie\", xp: 100 }\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:124
msgid ""
"**Note** — If your schema uses certain asynchronous APIs like `async` "
"[refinements](https://zod.dev/api#refinements) or "
"[transforms](https://zod.dev/api#transforms), you'll need to use the "
"`.parseAsync()` method instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:126
msgid ""
"const schema = z.string().refine(async (val) => val.length <= 8);\n"
"\n"
"await schema.parseAsync(\"hello\");\n"
"// => \"hello\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:133
msgid "Handling errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:135
msgid ""
"When validation fails, the `.parse()` method will throw a `ZodError` "
"instance with granular information about the validation issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:137
msgid ""
"try {\n"
"  Player.parse({ username: 42, xp: \"100\" });\n"
"} catch (err) {\n"
"  if (err instanceof z.ZodError) {\n"
"    err.issues;\n"
"    /* [\n"
"      {\n"
"        expected: 'string',\n"
"        code: 'invalid_type',\n"
"        path: [ 'username' ],\n"
"        message: 'Invalid input: expected string'\n"
"      },\n"
"      {\n"
"        expected: 'number',\n"
"        code: 'invalid_type',\n"
"        path: [ 'xp' ],\n"
"        message: 'Invalid input: expected number'\n"
"      }\n"
"    ] */\n"
"  }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:161
msgid ""
"To avoid a `try/catch` block, you can use the `.safeParse()` method to "
"get back a plain result object containing either the successfully parsed "
"data or a `ZodError`. The result type is a [discriminated "
"union](https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/narrowing.html"
"#discriminated-unions), so you can handle both cases conveniently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:163
msgid ""
"const result = Player.safeParse({ username: 42, xp: \"100\" });\n"
"if (!result.success) {\n"
"  result.error; // ZodError instance\n"
"} else {\n"
"  result.data; // { username: string; xp: number }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:172
msgid ""
"**Note** — If your schema uses certain asynchronous APIs like `async` "
"[refinements](#refine) or [transforms](#transform), you'll need to use "
"the `.safeParseAsync()` method instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:174
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"const schema = z.string().refine(async (val) => val.length <= 8);\n"
"\n"
"await schema.safeParseAsync(\"hello\");\n"
"// => { success: true; data: \"hello\" }\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:181
msgid "Inferring types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:183
msgid ""
"Zod infers a static type from your schema definitions. You can extract "
"this type with the `z.infer<>` utility and use it however you like."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:185
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"const Player = z.object({\n"
"  username: z.string(),\n"
"  xp: z.number(),\n"
"});\n"
"\n"
"// extract the inferred type\n"
"type Player = z.infer<typeof Player>;\n"
"\n"
"// use it in your code\n"
"const player: Player = { username: \"billie\", xp: 100 };\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:198
msgid ""
"In some cases, the input & output types of a schema can diverge. For "
"instance, the `.transform()` API can convert the input from one type to "
"another. In these cases, you can extract the input and output types "
"independently:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/zod/README.md:200
msgid ""
"const mySchema = z.string().transform((val) => val.length);\n"
"\n"
"type MySchemaIn = z.input<typeof mySchema>;\n"
"// => string\n"
"\n"
"type MySchemaOut = z.output<typeof mySchema>; // equivalent to "
"z.infer<typeof mySchema>\n"
"// number\n"
msgstr ""

